# Files a team-sync PR (branch `team-sync-*`) may touch. One path or folder per line.
# A folder (trailing /) covers everything under it. Globs are not supported (rejected).
# CI reads this list from the BASE branch: a new line counts only after it is merged. CI: scripts/ci/check_sync_scope.py.
#
# Deliberately NOT listed: project-specific rules that each repo keeps for itself
# (privacy rules, stub mode, docs/team/knowledge.md, docs/team/environment.md, .claude/settings.json
# (hooks may sit beside repo-specific permissions; CI checks each repo's copy with
# `lead_lock.py check-settings`), app code, contracts, plans, specs). Adding a line here is a deliberate decision.
CLAUDE.md
docs/team/lead.md
docs/team/lessons.md
.claude/agents/
.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/
.github/pull_request_template.md
docs/tasks/README.md
scripts/ci/check_task_scope.py
scripts/ci/check_alembic_heads.py
scripts/team/lead_lock.py
.github/workflows/team-checks.yml
docs/team/SYNC_FILES
